-- The aggregate seed: a `LIST OF NUMBER` field reduced by the prelude's list
-- combinators, plus one `map`-projected aggregate over a list of records.
--
-- The names here are the PRELUDE's, which are not the ones the M1 brief's IR
-- constraint 6 names: the prelude has `count`, not `length` (prelude.l4:119),
-- and has no `average` at all — `RAvg` exists only for the composite idiom
-- `sum xs DIVIDED BY count xs` over one and the same list, which is what
-- `average score` writes. `max`/`min` (prelude.l4:302,309) are the BINARY
-- combinators and are deliberately NOT aggregates; the list forms are
-- `maximum`/`minimum` (:336,345).
--
-- Two lowerings to read in the golden, because they differ on purpose:
--
--   * `total score`, `best score`, `average score` reduce a list that is
--     already a term (a projected field). An L4 list is data, not an open
--     predicate, so there is nothing to generate over and NO findall is
--     emitted — just `Out is sum(L)`.
--
--   * `basket total` reduces `map (GIVEN i YIELD i's price) (b's items)`. That
--     one does need a generator, so it becomes
--     `findall(Price, (member(I, Items), proj(I, price, Price)), L)` over the
--     synthesised `member` predicate — an RAuxiliary carrying RStructural on
--     argument 1, exactly like a user's own list recursion.
--
-- Each directive below carries its L4-oracle value on the line after it, as a
-- `-- L4 oracle ==>` comment produced by `l4 run scores.l4`. It is the
-- differential harness's expectation, and it lives outside the emitted program
-- on purpose (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R11) — one copy per directive, so there is
-- nothing here for a later edit to leave behind.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Student HAS
    scores IS A LIST OF NUMBER

DECLARE Item HAS
    price IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Basket HAS
    items IS A LIST OF Item

@export
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total score` s MEANS sum (s's scores)

@export
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A NUMBER
`best score` s MEANS maximum (s's scores)

@export
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A NUMBER
`average score` s MEANS sum (s's scores) DIVIDED BY count (s's scores)

@export
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `passes` IF `average score` s AT LEAST 50

@export
GIVEN b IS A Basket
GIVETH A NUMBER
`basket total` b MEANS sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's price) (b's items))

#EVAL `total score` (Student WITH scores IS LIST 80, 90, 70)
-- L4 oracle ==> 240

#EVAL `best score` (Student WITH scores IS LIST 80, 90, 70)
-- L4 oracle ==> 90

#EVAL `average score` (Student WITH scores IS LIST 80, 90, 70)
-- L4 oracle ==> 80

#EVAL `passes` (Student WITH scores IS LIST 80, 90, 70)
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

#EVAL `basket total` (Basket WITH items IS LIST (Item WITH price IS 10), (Item WITH price IS 25))
-- L4 oracle ==> 35
